[{:db/id "q-50371/selection/2e8fe9c6b49328f2f1392a57ec5c703aa3f30c2082e51a80e4121b631c734068" :answer/id #uuid "e82b5f7b-9696-54e1-b1a2-95d4e3187636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371/selection/ad5c4252bd1996cc27d5bd63044d0066bbda40a099f0133c27f31536558a3277" :answer/id #uuid "04998e9f-9e01-5cf2-a2ca-fc4b21c24bb9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}-{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,{t}^{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371/selection/5978c1b07168861d3544fce550c330a612a9e47e9da4338959ef4d5e147b4f90" :answer/id #uuid "8b48747b-b226-59e5-9900-3670f65971fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371/selection/287869dadb423a1d24ed00928dfb85974a190eaca1444b93f6f163104ac74dc6" :answer/id #uuid "0b9c019d-977f-5955-8493-e435a22e1136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371/selection/dc53cff62e1f5a169f4220d04b0d1848c4f2e3c30d36f56150b13b4441777848" :answer/id #uuid "f5b068f2-cbe7-5bf9-b70d-dadaf841489f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29ae8b6c-f927-5354-bb2a-e924f52b4e33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50371/selection/2e8fe9c6b49328f2f1392a57ec5c703aa3f30c2082e51a80e4121b631c734068" :answer-field/choices ["q-50371/selection/2e8fe9c6b49328f2f1392a57ec5c703aa3f30c2082e51a80e4121b631c734068" "q-50371/selection/ad5c4252bd1996cc27d5bd63044d0066bbda40a099f0133c27f31536558a3277" "q-50371/selection/5978c1b07168861d3544fce550c330a612a9e47e9da4338959ef4d5e147b4f90" "q-50371/selection/287869dadb423a1d24ed00928dfb85974a190eaca1444b93f6f163104ac74dc6" "q-50371/selection/dc53cff62e1f5a169f4220d04b0d1848c4f2e3c30d36f56150b13b4441777848"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50371" :question/id #uuid "607151f7-a0f9-522f-b6fe-540456f7af54" :question/math-academy-id "q-50371" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},\\,{t}^{5}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+1},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{e}^{t}({e}^{t}+1)-{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{5},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{t}+1)}^{2}},\\,5{t}^{4}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-50371/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50371"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347617/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8c44c3ea-3ebf-5ee5-af0a-8110ad679376" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347617/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf779698-c2ba-5641-af73-001c287ae21b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347617/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-347617/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347617" :question/id #uuid "69e2c430-6329-572d-a61d-182cbabbb01a" :question/math-academy-id "q-347617" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨7-3t,\\,2{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(1)|?$\n\n$|{r}^{′}(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=7-3t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=-3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=2{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=4t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=4(1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-3)}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347617/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c5abf2d8-c8a4-5524-9322-11275d512b49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4afc81d1-1742-588d-af02-c1806d222f27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a82e46e-061b-598b-9edc-e29e6ec5b771" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349469/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-349469/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-349469/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "04818994-d6d9-5b40-984b-58d918b92e36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "bdebd735-4aed-511f-9364-c21a3d0dde07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349469/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-349469/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349469" :question/id #uuid "18dc3f26-327b-53a4-8232-4e313a8b13d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-349469" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(0)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(0)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{2t}(t+1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =(2{e}^{2t})(t+1)+{e}^{2t}(1) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(t+1)+{e}^{2t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(0)=2{e}^{2\\cdot 0}(0+1)+{e}^{2\\cdot 0}=3.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{9-{t}^{2}}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(0)=-\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{9-{0}^{2}}}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{x}^{′}(0),\\,{y}^{′}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349469/field-1" "q-349469/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349469"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection/93981643e8761ffb9043d7b035af2cc3e75344b80cd472dec7d506dc2b17db76" :answer/id #uuid "c25ec7de-12af-529c-af44-a22fc24a0151" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection/f47dbad8fcd696327dd6bd91c27d7d76ac4a106b814da4a7d7d0ce84b8f334e5" :answer/id #uuid "3a27fa3f-430b-59a5-bfa0-477b70d9a00b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection/7855d8411e35fc991e718f705577aefee2164b433b78779a602d25f7fc7bcc74" :answer/id #uuid "71d744fe-2f62-5cf8-8f81-87a43426ed95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection/0eaf55fb6b5e887e659d1abd9fd489460b3908d7a4b4ce67b22a46c37fea2b69" :answer/id #uuid "3e066582-5eca-5419-a495-6965c1800f41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨\\frac{3}{4},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection/e277a18c959cdb703768dc3389ac63351e04ed767292f35e0b4517bcdf7505bb" :answer/id #uuid "0534d891-006d-5d29-a9ad-aa1a973dfd63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b53136bb-c75f-5654-a83c-966336d9efc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50409/selection/e277a18c959cdb703768dc3389ac63351e04ed767292f35e0b4517bcdf7505bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-50409/selection/93981643e8761ffb9043d7b035af2cc3e75344b80cd472dec7d506dc2b17db76" "q-50409/selection/f47dbad8fcd696327dd6bd91c27d7d76ac4a106b814da4a7d7d0ce84b8f334e5" "q-50409/selection/7855d8411e35fc991e718f705577aefee2164b433b78779a602d25f7fc7bcc74" "q-50409/selection/0eaf55fb6b5e887e659d1abd9fd489460b3908d7a4b4ce67b22a46c37fea2b69" "q-50409/selection/e277a18c959cdb703768dc3389ac63351e04ed767292f35e0b4517bcdf7505bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50409" :question/id #uuid "189c2727-12a4-5484-ae84-df807a41b9e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-50409" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{sin}^{3}⁡t,\\,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={sin}^{3}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={cos}^{2}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4},\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50409/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50409"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50373/selection/c7305719b4d830df8a95c3223f827c1adbbbe00055debbe4fe9ce53012e1f2c4" :answer/id #uuid "7d81d374-3be8-5dad-bad8-7bbfcbcd0fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50373/selection/202d6c98eb96cd8ea27970da6a90c1f3e37a304551b6a11a90f4317764062f25" :answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50373/selection/49a553732b8b66437d6188187b1ea5b0d3831411cfb297f8f4ef841aac4c3cdf" :answer/id #uuid "a02992c9-bb0d-53e8-8eee-9ab879a36726" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50373/selection/63bc5d3a5a8fb167c9116a5312cddda5b